hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-25 = cons "The paper's §1 gives the account of what an observation warrants that knowledge graphs have lacked. Let H be the" (cons "admissible histories of a process and o : H → O an observation. A reading y doesn't identify a history. It" (cons "determines the fiber of compatible histories (equation 1.1):" (cons "" (cons "  Fib_o(y) := Σ_{h:H} (o(h) = y)," (cons "" (cons "and what the reading warrants about a proposed conclusion P is a construction over that whole fiber (equation 1.3):" (cons "" (cons "  Warrants(y, P) := Π_{(h,p):Fib_o(y)} P(h)." (cons "" nil)))))))))
